From 2d7f5d09fc22ae318eefc0cf138d05a81fc57c2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lyanteo <lyanteo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:19:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: vayu: add stubs for the stock dtbo overlay

The Qualcomm bootloader applies the vendor overlay from the dtbo partition
(board-id 47, model "VAYU") on top of the kernel DTB and aborts the boot
when a referenced label is missing. The stock Infinity-X 3.12 dtbo
references 118 labels that only exist in the vendor 4.14 tree.

Provide empty nodes for those labels in a disabled container without a
compatible, so the overlay applies cleanly and its content is never used.
The DTB must be built with symbols (DTC_FLAGS=-@).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0192C5wPw4AwnF1EyMXZJ5bh
